# ALL.mask -- CEO-409 line masks for this package, declared beside the data (RULES.md; ceo CEO-409, CEO-1344, CEO-1351).
# FORMAT: entry<TAB>pattern<TAB>reason; pattern is a python regex, L<n>, or ORACLE-ONLY:<exact line>. An empty reason is REFUSED.
# Read by the package runner through util_apply_ceo409_mask.py, the harness's own read_mask_sidecar()/apply_line_mask().
#
# ⭐ ORACLE-IDENTITY (ceo CEO-1344, 2026-09-27; CEO-1351, 2026-09-28): HOST() with no argument answers the implementation's own identity --
# sbl -bf prints "host(): x86-64:unix :Macro SPITBOL 15.01 #" -- the ORACLE'S OWN INTERNAL STATE, the same class as its memory lines. SCRIP
# does not impersonate SPITBOL and carries no permanent debt for it, so that one line is masked on both sides and the program grades on
# everything else it prints (host(0)). host prints two lines, so the one mask is half the fixture: a row whose reason cites CEO-1344 is
# exempt from guardrail 4 while at least one line stays unmasked, and is admitted only as a content regex (CEO-1351).
host	^host\(\): .*$	CEO-1344 oracle identity: HOST() answers the implementation's own name ("x86-64:unix :Macro SPITBOL 15.01 #" under sbl -bf), which no program computes and SCRIP does not impersonate
gcbuster	^[0-9]+$	CEO-1344 oracle identity: OUTPUT = COLLECT() prints the free storage the implementation's own allocator holds after a collection (84665 and 84663 under sbl -bf, about 7151824 under SCRIP, which runs a different collector over a different heap), a quantity no program computes (ceo CEO-1397)
gcbuster	^(BASEMEM|TOPMEM) = [0-9]+$	CEO-1344 oracle identity: HOST(-1,2) and HOST(-1,3) answer the heap's base and top ADDRESSES in the implementation's own address space, which differ on every run of either; SCRIP answers its own (ceo CEO-1397, SCRIP src/runtime/core/core.c HOST -1 arm)
gcbuster	^(STACKSIZ|STACKCUR|STACKMAX) = [0-9]+$	CEO-1344 oracle identity: HOST(-1,4), (-1,5) and (-1,7) answer the stack's usable size, the bytes in use and the high-water mark of the implementation's own stack -- sbl subtracts a private 400-byte safety margin from its size and counts its interpreter's frames, SCRIP answers the declared -s and its emitted frames; test_gate_sno_host_minus_one_answers_the_memory_statistics.sh pins that every selector answers and the relations hold (ceo CEO-1397)
